The turn count of every rework (round-2) worker session in the loop archive, and its distribution.
Taken 2026-11-07 in the change root, over /home/tim/projects/NaviVeylin/.pi/issue-loop/items/*/events.jsonl
(725 event streams). A session is the rework round when the first user message names worker-prompt-round2.

  for f in */events.jsonl; do
    jq -r 'if .type=="session" then "S"
           elif (.type=="message_start" and (.message.role=="user")) then
             (if ((.message.content|tostring)|test("worker-prompt-round2")) then "R2" else "U" end)
           elif .type=="turn_end" then "T" else empty end' "$f"
  done > /tmp/r2.stream
  awk '{...}' /tmp/r2.stream | sort -n | awk '{a[NR]=$1} END{ ... p95 ... }'

Output (the last line is the one the change quotes):

  42737   (lines of the reduced stream)
  109     (rework sessions)
  n=109 min=11 median=60 p95=100 max=197

The p95 is the population the recorded bound LOOP_CHILD_TURNS_MAX_WORKER_REWORK=100 is derived from
(guidelines/BacklogTooling.md section 11: "A value sits at or above the archive's p95 for its role").

Archive-wide role split for the same archive (python3 tools/loop-spend.py --items .pi/issue-loop/items --json,
2026-11-07): reviewer 284 sessions / 10 160 turns, worker 441 sessions / 30 884 turns — the rework round is
charged to "worker" there, which is the accounting this change makes separately possible.
